WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.068
-Our next guest is a very funny
actress you know from shows

00:00:03.068 --> 00:00:05.037
such as "Cougar Town"
and "Freaks and Geeks."

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:07.773
She stars in the second season
of "Girls5eva,"

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.375
which is streaming now
on Peacock.

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:10.477
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.578
-Kev.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.515
I'm going on a tour.
You're gonna stay with Stevia.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.449
-No, I'm not to be trusted!

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:18.985
-You'll figure it out.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.887
Just like I had to
when you went to Tampa.

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:23.523
-Ugh!
-Hey!

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.691
Listen to me.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.726
Be her best friend,
not her parent.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.295
Win her heart
through possessions.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:33.299
And find out what she's up to by
posing as an older, very cool,

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:37.203
CGI shapewear CEO on TikTok.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.739
I'll give you the account
and the password I made up.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.274
Also --
-Can I get paper?

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.909
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.011
our friend Busy Philipps,
everybody!

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.679
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:53.486 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:53.486 --> 00:01:00.326 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.461
Welcome to the show, Busy.
-Hi!

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:03.496
-I'm so happy to have you back.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.531
-Oh, my God, I'm so happy
to be here.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.100
-And you're a New Yorker
this time.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.235
-This is it, Seth.
I live in New York.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.437
-You live in New York City now.
-I do!

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.172
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:15.141
-We last talked via Zoom
in 2020,

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.276
and you were still
a Los Angelino.

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.512
-Here's what I'm gonna say.
-Yeah.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.947
-None of this was
on my bingo card.

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:25.651
-Okay.
-If you had paid anyone that

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:30.956
knows me millions of dollars to
say, "Will Busy ever live

00:01:30.956 --> 00:01:32.959
in New York," they would say no.
-Yeah.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.728
-And they would lose the bet,
but here we are.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.897
Because Tina Fey called me
and said,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.231
"Do you want to do
this TV show?"

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:41.500
And I was like,
"Yeah, obviously."

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.669
-And then you --
I mean, you could have gone back

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:45.705
in between seasons.
You dug it!

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.907
Admit you dig it.
-Here's what I'm gonna say.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:51.377
We have teens now,
like preteen teenagers.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:54.280
-Yeah.
-And I really feel like New York

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:58.284
offers a thing
that Los Angeles doesn't,

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:01.754
which isn't to say that L.A.
doesn't have culture, but...

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:02.989
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.458
...it's just
a different culture.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.792
Do you know what I mean?

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:09.229
-I think the thing about
New York culture is if you just

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.764
walk down the street, you're
gonna get a fair share of it.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.266
-You get it.
I've gotten it in my face.

00:02:14.266 --> 00:02:16.402
-Yep.
-I've gotten it on my shoes.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.837
I kicked a rat once, I mean.
-You did?

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:21.440
Did you apologize?
-Oh, always.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.675
I'm like, "Sir, sir,
I'm so sorry, sir."

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.577
-Because the rats in your
neighborhood know

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.913
the other rats, and then if you
get a bad reputation --

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:27.914
-Yeah.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.416
-Now, your kids,
Birdie and Cricket.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.685
-Yes.
-So, they are enjoying it?

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.255
-Yeah, they love it.
-Okay. They don't miss L.A.?

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:38.090
-No, they actually,
like, don't miss L.A.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.493
-That's really nice.
-Yeah, it is nice.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:44.296
-I've asked about this. Have you
introduced them to past work?

00:02:44.296 --> 00:02:45.865
I mean, do they watch
"Girls5eva"?

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.967
-Yeah. Well, no. Well, okay.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.002
So, you guys know -- I mean,

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:53.539
I've been an actor since I was
like a kid, basically.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.441
I was 19 years old when I did
"Freaks and Geeks."

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:59.311
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:02.448
I am about to turn 43!

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.116
And that's true.

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:06.018
That's true,
I'm about to turn 43.

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:10.589
Do you find that, like -- I just
almost said 41 because I turned

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:13.292
40 right before the pandemic,
and in my head I just was like,

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:14.727
"I'm about to turn 41."

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:17.496
And you wouldn't have known,
and I could have just done it.

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:18.797
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:20.500
-Anyway.
-They should have passed a law

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.502
that none of the birthdays
during the pandemic counted.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.236
-I don't think they did!
-Yeah.

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:25.405
-I mean, they didn't count.
-Everybody's like,

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:27.473
"Forgive student loans."
Forgive my two birthdays!

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.107
[ Laughter ]
-Seth!

00:03:29.107 --> 00:03:30.943
Forgive my two birthdays.

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:33.812
So, I'm about to turn 41,
I've been acting since I was 19,

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:36.616
and I have these two kids.

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:40.019
And I've been trying --
My kids love TV.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.854
They love shows.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.856
And Birdie, especially
if you have a teenager,

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:47.393
you know this -- like, they love
to watch old shows.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.661
And I'm like,
"Guess what I'm on."

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.929
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:52.732
I'm on "Dawson's Creek"
and "Freaks and Geeks."

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.202
Not interested.
Not interested.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.503
-No, really?
-No, no.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.671
-Because they don't
like the show

00:03:58.671 --> 00:03:59.738
or because they don't want to
see you?

00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:01.107
-It's me.
-Okay.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:03.142
-100% it's me.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.543
I tried to show Cricket,

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:08.280
who's our almost 9-year-old,
"Girls5eva."

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.683
She watched it for two seconds.
You guys just saw the clip.

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.485
I hope you're watching the show
because it's really funny.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:17.122
And she said, "Your voice is
really weird on this.

00:04:17.122 --> 00:04:18.591
I don't like it at all."

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.594
And I was like, "Okay."

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:25.965
But so anyways, so Birdie's been
like, emphatically no.

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:29.034
Has watched -- The last time we
talked, it was Birdie's birthday

00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:30.936
in the pandemic, and I got all
my friends who are on

00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:33.038
"Brooklyn Nine-Nine" to, like,

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:35.407
do a little video
for Birdie at home.

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:38.844
That's because I've been in TV
since I was a child.

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:41.280
I know everyone.
-That's very nice.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.815
-Anyway.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:44.783
And like, yeah, so she's watched
"The Office,"

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.519
"Brooklyn Nine-Nine,"
"Parks and Rec."

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.622
She loves you.
She loves everyone except for,

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.990
like, hasn't watched anything
I'm on.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.225
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.860
And I've tried,
and she won't do it,

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.427
and then last night --
they won't do it.

00:04:55.427 --> 00:04:57.663
Last night,
Birdie had a friend over.

00:04:57.663 --> 00:05:00.499
And I invited them to come down
for dinner, and they did

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:02.235
and of course sat
in front of the TV.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:05.237
And I was, like, preparing
things in the kitchen

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:06.806
and then I heard the theme
from "Freaks and Geeks."

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:07.806
-Wow.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:09.909
-And I was like,
"Is it happening?"

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.877
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:15.714
Like, "Be cool, be cool."

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.150
"What are you guys watching?!"

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.483
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.483 --> 00:05:22.822
And Birdie was like,
"Bevan wanted to see you on TV,

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.023
so we turned on
'Freaks and Geeks.'"

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.392
And I was like,
"That's cool, yeah."

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.226
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.226 --> 00:05:29.661
"And it was so weird.

00:05:29.661 --> 00:05:32.064
That's me. I was 19, g--"

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:34.200
And Birdie goes --
and I'm not kidding you --

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.135
"You talk really weird
on this show."

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:37.903
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.472
And I was like, "Okay."

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:42.308
And so anyway, they watched it,
and then at a certain point,

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.377
the girl came to do my nails
for your show.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:47.780
And I was like, "Okay, I got to
go get my nails done."

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.181
And Birdie just took
the controller

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.449
and was like,
"We've seen enough."

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:52.285
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.819
-You got to wait for you
to leave.

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:55.120
You were leaving the room
anyway!

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.856
Wait for you to leave.
-It was the point!

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.092
You know, the cruelty
is the point!

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:00.660
-Oh, yes!

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.529
I hope -- Well, you know,
hopefully she's gonna look past

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.798
the fact that she hates seeing
you on TV to watch me tonight

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:08.501
and will hear that you're being
very mean to your mother.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.102
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:11.804
Now, you know, one of --

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:14.106
We talked about culture,
but obviously Broadway.

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:16.743
And I'm wondering if Birdie
or Cricket likes going to

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:18.411
Broadway shows
and if you take them.

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:21.147
-Well, I would, but again,
it's been a pandemic.

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:23.316
And so, and I've been on
a TV show

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:25.651
and I don't want to get people
sick with COVID.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.319
-Right, of course.

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:30.355
-But I did -- Like, things are
opening back up

00:06:30.355 --> 00:06:31.657
and we actually got COVID,

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.092
so now I feel a little bit
better about it.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.427
And you know that feel--

00:06:35.427 --> 00:06:37.496
I mean, you all know
that feeling, right?

00:06:37.496 --> 00:06:38.630
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:40.900
-Well, the right after
is pretty not bad.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.502
-Well, that's what it --
that's where we're at.

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:43.736
-Oh, you're the right after.

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.838
Oh, my God, live your best life,
yeah.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:48.741
-So, I've been wanting to see
"A Strange Loop,"

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:51.443
which is this amazing show
that just won a Tony.

00:06:51.443 --> 00:06:52.678
-Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.713
-And I knew nothing about it,
but I was like,

00:06:54.713 --> 00:06:56.215
"Just got to see the show,"
and so I bought tickets

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:57.383
and I'm like, "Birdie, we're
going to the show

00:06:57.383 --> 00:07:00.019
on Saturday night,"
and I saw on Instagram

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:02.021
that Sara Bareilles,
who's on "Girls5eva" with me

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:04.856
and also is just a big star
in her own right,

00:07:04.856 --> 00:07:07.426
and I just follow her on
Instagram for that reason,

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:09.996
was at the show, and so I texted
her, "Oh, I'm so excited.

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:11.530
I'm taking Birdie tonight."

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:15.334
And Sara wrote back,
"Dot, dot, dot."

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.236
And I was like,
"What's that mean?"

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:21.107
And Sara was like, "Do you know
what it's about, babe?

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.808
It's, like, pretty mature."

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:24.410
And I was like,
"Well, Birdie's like a teenager.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.544
It's going to be fine."

00:07:25.544 --> 00:07:26.845
And then Sara calls me
and she's like,

00:07:26.845 --> 00:07:28.915
"Uh, no, Busy. Um...

00:07:28.915 --> 00:07:31.884
Like, in the show, in the first
song, they say there's going to

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:33.352
be butt[bleep] onstage."

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.921
[ Audience ohhs ]
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:37.323
They deliver!

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:38.924
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.924 --> 00:07:41.827
-They don't over-promise.
-They don't disappoint!

00:07:41.827 --> 00:07:44.163
And I was like, "Oh.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:45.898
Oh, no. Well, what do I do?"

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:48.767
Well, Birdie watches
"Bridgerton," but not with me.

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:51.770
[ Laughter ]
So I had this whole dilemma.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.105
And so then I was like,
you know what?

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:54.339
Communication is key.

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:57.776
I'm like, "Birdie, the show that
I'm really excited

00:07:57.776 --> 00:08:00.079
to take you to,
this is the situation.

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.514
Sara Bareilles told me
that this happens onstage,"

00:08:02.514 --> 00:08:04.049
and Birdie's like,
"Yeah, no, we're good.

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:05.284
I'm not going to go
to that with you."

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:07.186
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.620
That was it?
-And that was it.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.088
And then I took my friend,
and it was great.

00:08:10.088 --> 00:08:11.790
-That's great.
-And it's an amazing show.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:16.061
-Alright. That's great.
But maybe not for new teenagers.

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:19.331
-Well, I would just say that
like we don't watch "Bridgerton"

00:08:19.331 --> 00:08:21.267
sitting next to each other.
Do you know what I mean?

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:24.069
-Yeah.
-No child, no matter how, like,

00:08:24.069 --> 00:08:28.207
evolved and communicative
you are with your teenagers,

00:08:28.207 --> 00:08:32.111
wants to watch sex
with your mom,

00:08:32.111 --> 00:08:34.080
even if your mom is me
and you're so cool.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.547
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.547 --> 00:08:39.351
-Well, if there's any message
to take away, let it be that.

00:08:39.351 --> 00:08:42.654
That's parenting advice
from Busy Philipps, everybody!

00:08:42.654 --> 00:08:45.391
"Girls5eva" is available now
on Peacock.

00:08:45.391 --> 00:08:47.226
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

